  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Request path",
      "items": [
        "The Submit button first saves the draft (PUT), then calls POST /api/v1/report-slots/{id}/submit",
        "Gate failures stop at 401/403; submit checks stop at 409/422 before db.commit(), so nothing is saved",
        "One commit stores the new status, the audit entry, the report.submitted outbox row and a pending similarity check"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Cache and fallbacks",
      "items": [
        "No HTTP or Redis cache exists; system settings are read from the database on each request",
        "The only hit/miss is the embedding model held in process memory; it is None when AI is off or loading failed",
        "The draft text stays in localStorage until the server has it and is removed after a successful save or submit",
        "A failed or model-less check is saved as failed; similarity_retry re-runs it every 5 minutes, up to 3 attempts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Asynchronous work",
      "items": [
        "The similarity check runs in a Starlette background task after the 200 is sent, in its own session",
        "The outbox row is the event: the deliver_notifications job emails and pushes it to the supervisor within about a minute",
        "There is no distributed tracing; failures go to the Python log and job results to job_runs"
      ]
    }
  ]
